id: remote-control
name: Remote Control
kind: gear
tags: tech
craftDC: Expert
# "Select an Item (Bomb/Collar/Vehicle/Battle Jacket) you possess for it to be connected to."
# Only the Bomb exists here yet; the others join this list when they do.
connects: bomb
# "For a Bomb, you can spend 1 Action to trigger that Bomb."
placeCost: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Connected to one of your Items when you get it: trigger a Bomb, or set off a Collar, for
  an Action; pilot a Vehicle or Battle Jacket from afar.
text: >
  Remote Control [Tech]: A portable device capable of wireless communication with the
  advanced computational systems of a Battle Jacket, allowing for remote operation.
  –Craft DC: Expert
  –Effects: Upon creating this Basic Item, select an Item (Bomb/Collar/Vehicle/Battle
  Jacket) you possess for it to be connected to. This Remote Control can be used to control
  that Item, allowing you to spend your Actions as if you are Piloting a Vehicle or Battle
  Jacket that can be controlled with this Remote Control. For a Bomb, you can spend 1 Action
  to trigger that Bomb. For a Collar Accessory, you can spend 1 Action to trigger the effects
  of that Accessory.

  You cannot use this effect if the Vehicle or Battle Jacket has a Pilot.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Connected when it is given: the character picks one of their own Items it can control, and
# the connection can be changed on the Remote Control afterwards.
#
# A Bomb set to Remote Controlled is set off from here and nowhere else: its own row offers
# no Detonate, and this one offers Trigger, for an Action, once the Bomb is placed.
#
# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Collar, Vehicles and Battle Jackets are not in this system yet, so there is nothing of
# theirs to connect to - and piloting from afar, and "you cannot use this effect if the
# Vehicle or Battle Jacket has a Pilot", wait with them.
